From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kan Zhu <kanzhu@cs.washington.edu>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:48:44 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] alignment: record every DP forward with a forward ordinal

Under data parallelism an idle rank runs a dummy forward on every
busy-loop pass in which it ran no real step, so that its DP/EP
collectives pair with its peers'. The alignment iteration record was
written only for real steps, so idle ranks' forwards were missing and a
consumer had to pair ranks by wall clock, which the asynchronous
observation windows do not support.

Schema 5 adds forward_ordinal (per-rank count of model forwards, dummies
included, from 0), is_dummy and dp_rank. A step that runs a forward
(scheduled tokens > 0) takes the next ordinal when it is dispatched; a
DP dummy forward takes one and writes a zero-work record. A 0-token
step runs no forward and takes none. Equal ordinals on two ranks are
the same global step: each forward syncs its batch across DP ranks
(coordinate_batch_across_dp / dispatch_cg_and_sync_dp).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
