-`VibeSimAlignmentIteration` records. Existing
+`--enable-logging-iteration-details` for schema-v5
+`VibeSimAlignmentIteration` records. Schema 5 adds `forward_ordinal`,
+`is_dummy`, `dp_rank` and `max_forwards_in_flight` (the batch-queue depth: how
+many forwards a rank can have launched but not finished), and records every model forward of the EngineCore
+loop: a real step (scheduled tokens > 0) and, under data parallelism, each
+dummy forward an idle rank runs to join its peers' collectives (zero work,
+`iteration_index: null`). A 0-token step runs no forward and records none.
+Every DP rank runs exactly one forward per busy-loop pass while a wave runs
+(both runners sync the batch across DP ranks inside each forward), so equal
+`forward_ordinal`s on two ranks are the same global step. Existing
 `VLLM_VIBESIM_TOKEN_TRACE_*` and `VLLM_VIBESIM_ROUTING_TRACE_*` switches apply
 to both model runners. Dumps can synchronize/copy GPU data; collect them in
 the separate evidence pass, not in timing captures. The token dump uses actual
